# The 600-cell and the 120-cell, the two exceptional regular polychora of four-dimensional space, modeled and proved by
# the kernel. The 600-cell {3,3,5} is built from 600 regular tetrahedral cells, five meeting around each edge: it has
# 120 vertices, 720 edges, 1200 triangular faces, and 600 tetrahedral cells. The 120-cell {5,3,3} is built from 120
# dodecahedral cells, three meeting around each edge: it has 600 vertices, 1200 edges, 720 pentagonal faces, and 120
# dodecahedral cells. They are DUAL: one's f-vector is the other's reversed, vertex against cell and edge against face.
# Both carry the H4 Coxeter symmetry, the non-crystallographic reflection group of order 14400, the largest finite
# symmetry group in four dimensions, generated by four reflections with the bonds {3,3,5}. H4 is non-crystallographic
# because it does not preserve any lattice: its symmetry uses the golden ratio phi = (1 + root five) / 2, an irrational
# number, so no integer grid is fixed. The 120 vertices of the 600-cell are exactly the 120 unit ICOSIANS, the unit
# quaternions whose coordinates are built from phi, and these 120 quaternions form the binary icosahedral group 2I, the
# double cover of the icosahedral rotation group. Because the vertex coordinates are irrational (they involve phi) this
# file does NOT construct the 120 points. Instead it models the COMBINATORIAL face lattice, the f-vector of each
# polytope as integer facts, and proves the genuine structural content: that the duality is a rank-reversing involution
# carrying one f-vector onto the other, and that the four-dimensional Euler characteristic of each polytope is zero. The
# five tetrahedra around an edge of the 600-cell, the final 5 of {3,3,5}, are modeled as an order-five cycle and proved
# to return after five steps.

load @term/seed/atom/flag
  find flag

# The four ranks of the face lattice of a 4-polytope: a vertex (rank 0), an edge (rank 1), a face (rank 2), and a cell
# (rank 3). Every element of either polytope is one of these four kinds.
form element-kind
  case vertex
  case edge
  case face
  case cell

# THE F-VECTOR OF THE 600-CELL {3,3,5}: how many elements of each rank it has. 120 vertices, 720 edges, 1200 triangular
# faces, 600 tetrahedral cells. These are integer facts about the combinatorics of the polytope, returned per rank.
task count-600-cell
  take r, like element-kind
  like integer
  fork case, read r
    case vertex
      send back
        code 120
    case edge
      send back
        code 720
    case face
      send back
        code 1200
    case cell
      send back
        code 600

# THE F-VECTOR OF THE 120-CELL {5,3,3}: 600 vertices, 1200 edges, 720 pentagonal faces, 120 dodecahedral cells. Each
# entry is the 600-cell's entry at the DUAL rank, which is the duality proved below. Integer facts.
task count-120-cell
  take r, like element-kind
  like integer
  fork case, read r
    case vertex
      send back
        code 600
    case edge
      send back
        code 1200
    case face
      send back
        code 720
    case cell
      send back
        code 120

# THE DUALITY MAP ON RANKS: reverse the face lattice. In four dimensions duality swaps vertex with cell (rank 0 with
# rank 3) and edge with face (rank 1 with rank 2). This is the geometric polarity that carries the 600-cell to the
# 120-cell, realized here as the rank-reversal permutation.
task dual-rank
  take r, like element-kind
  like element-kind
  fork case, read r
    case vertex
      send back
        make cell
    case edge
      send back
        make face
    case face
      send back
        make edge
    case cell
      send back
        make vertex

# THE FIVE TETRAHEDRA AROUND AN EDGE of the 600-cell, the final 5 of {3,3,5}: five regular tetrahedral cells meet around
# each edge. We name them as a five-element cycle, the local patch around one edge, so the five-fold meeting is a
# constructed structure and not a bare count.
form edge-tetrahedron
  case first
  case second
  case third
  case fourth
  case fifth

# The cyclic order of the five tetrahedra around an edge: going around the edge visits them in turn and returns to the
# first. This is the order-five rotation that the five-around-an-edge fact means geometrically.
task around-edge
  take t, like edge-tetrahedron
  like edge-tetrahedron
  fork case, read t
    case first
      send back
        make second
    case second
      send back
        make third
    case third
      send back
        make fourth
    case fourth
      send back
        make fifth
    case fifth
      send back
        make first

# DUAL-RANK IS AN INVOLUTION: dual-rank (dual-rank r) = r, for every rank. Reversing the face lattice twice returns the
# original rank, so duality is a polarity of order two. Proved over all four ranks.
rule dual-rank-is-an-involution
  seat r, like element-kind
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call dual-rank
        call dual-rank
          read r
      read r
  fold r

# THE 600-CELL AND 120-CELL ARE DUAL: the 120-cell's count at the dual rank equals the 600-cell's count at the original
# rank, count-120-cell (dual-rank r) = count-600-cell r, for every rank. This is the exact structural statement of the
# duality: reversing the f-vector of one gives the other. At rank vertex it says the 120-cell's cell count (120) equals
# the 600-cell's vertex count (120), and so on through every rank. Proved over all four ranks.
rule the-two-polytopes-are-dual
  seat r, like element-kind
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call count-120-cell
        call dual-rank
          read r
      call count-600-cell
        read r
  fold r

# FIVE TETRAHEDRA GO AROUND AN EDGE: applying the around-edge step five times returns to the start, around-edge five
# times is the identity, for each of the five tetrahedra. This is the five-fold meeting of tetrahedral cells around
# every edge, the final 5 of the Schlafli symbol {3,3,5}, proved as the order-five cycle of the local patch.
rule five-tetrahedra-around-an-edge
  seat t, like edge-tetrahedron
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call around-edge
        call around-edge
          call around-edge
            call around-edge
              call around-edge
                read t
      read t
  fold t

# THE EULER CHARACTERISTIC OF THE 600-CELL IS ZERO: vertices minus edges plus faces minus cells equals zero, the
# four-dimensional Euler relation. 120 - 720 + 1200 - 600 = 0. Every convex 4-polytope satisfies this alternating sum,
# the four-dimensional analog of the familiar V - E + F = 2 for solids. The four entries are the 600-cell's f-vector,
# discharged by builtin arithmetic.
hold euler-characteristic-of-600-cell-is-zero
  call is-equal
    code 0
    call subtract
      call add
        call subtract
          code 120
          code 720
        code 1200
      code 600

# THE EULER CHARACTERISTIC OF THE 120-CELL IS ZERO: 600 - 1200 + 720 - 120 = 0, the same four-dimensional Euler
# relation for the dual polytope, the 120-cell's f-vector discharged by builtin arithmetic.
hold euler-characteristic-of-120-cell-is-zero
  call is-equal
    code 0
    call subtract
      call add
        call subtract
          code 600
          code 1200
        code 720
      code 120

# THE H4 SYMMETRY GROUP HAS ORDER 14400, the largest finite symmetry group in four dimensions, shared by the 600-cell
# and the 120-cell. It is non-crystallographic, built on the golden ratio, and factors as the 120 vertices of the
# 600-cell times the order-120 binary icosahedral stabilizer structure: 14400 = 120 * 120. The 120 vertices are the
# 120 unit icosians, which as unit quaternions form the binary icosahedral group 2I, the double cover of the order-60
# icosahedral rotation group. Stated here as the constructed factorization.
hold order-of-h4-is-vertices-times-icosian-group
  call is-equal
    code 14400
    call multiply
      code 120
      code 120

# THE 600-CELL HAS 120 VERTICES, the order of the binary icosahedral group 2I: each unit icosian is one vertex, and the
# 120 icosians are closed under quaternion multiplication into the group 2I, the double cover of the icosahedral
# rotation group of order 60. Stated as the constructed numeral, the count read off the f-vector.
hold six-hundred-cell-vertex-count-is-the-icosian-group-order
  call is-equal
    code 120
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 60
